{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTAwNzA=","login":"seveibar","name":"Severin Ibarluzea","databaseId":1910070}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTAwNzA=","is_bot":false,"login":"seveibar","name":"Severin Ibarluzea"},"body":"Create the Arduino Nano on tscircuit snippets.\n\nhttps://store-usa.arduino.cc/products/arduino-nano?queryID=undefined&selectedStore=us\n\n/bounty $100\n\nTo get the bounty, you just need to edit the README and add a link to your Arduino Nano.\n\nWe will actually order your board and test it!\n\nPlease share your work on discord and we will help you with design issues.\n\ntscircuit is still in active development, and this is a fairly difficult board, you may need the team to help build features as you go, stay active on the discord- we're here to help!","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF886-O-a1","author":{"login":"swastikCommits"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2025-08-15T14:10:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3191596725","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887IYww8","author":{"login":"nehaaprasad"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n@seveibar \nplease check it out!","createdAt":"2025-10-02T15:45:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3361934396","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887kNxkZ","author":{"login":"ainanasolo2005-commits"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-01-31T16:47:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3828816153","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887r5du_","author":{"login":"jdhruv1503"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-02-25T08:45:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3957709759","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887r5h28","author":{"login":"jdhruv1503"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-02-25T08:48:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3957726652","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887r7cHv","author":{"login":"jdhruv1503"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\nSubmitting PR #2338 for bounty. Circuit ready for production testing.","createdAt":"2026-02-25T10:18:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-3958227439","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887voRP7","author":{"login":"kacperkostrzab"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I'm a TypeScript Developer with a strong background in structured data and component-based architecture. I'd love to take on the task of building the Arduino Nano model within tscircuit.\n\nI have experience in creating precise technical layouts and understand the pinout and form factor of the Arduino Nano. I will ensure that the implementation is accurate, follows the tscircuit standards, and is well-documented for other users.\n\nI can start working on this immediately. Could you please assign this task to me?","createdAt":"2026-03-09T00:03:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4020311035","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887v6aQC","author":{"login":"CuboYe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim 328\n\nClaiming territory for a scoped fix attempt now. If maintainer preference differs, I can adapt quickly.","createdAt":"2026-03-09T16:33:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"SPAM","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4025066498","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887wxJU1","author":{"login":"Nicolas-Rozas"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nImplemented a complete Arduino Nano circuit including:\n- ATmega328P (TQFP-32) main MCU + CH340G (SOP-16) USB-to-serial converter\n- 16MHz crystal for MCU, 12MHz crystal for CH340G with load capacitors\n- Status LEDs: PWR (green), TX/RX/L (yellow) with 1k current-limiting resistors\n- Reset button with 10k pull-up resistor and 100nF debounce capacitor\n- Full decoupling capacitor network (100nF + 10uF bulk caps for both ICs)\n- 2x15 pin headers and ICSP 2x3 header\n- README updated with link to the snippet\n\nPR: https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/2565","createdAt":"2026-03-11T13:58:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4039415093","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887yL2hX","author":{"login":"kira-autonoma"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nComplete Arduino Nano V3.0 circuit implementation with ATmega328P-AU, CH340G USB-serial, AMS1117-5.0 voltage regulator, crystals, LEDs, reset circuit, DTR auto-reset, ICSP header, pin headers, and full decoupling network. JLCPCB part numbers included.\n\nPR: https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/2653","createdAt":"2026-03-15T15:09:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4063193175","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF887yjV1F","author":{"login":"CuboYe"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nPost-1081 ROI activation from refreshed shortlist.\n\nExecution plan (test-first, non-duplicate):\n1) Audit currently open Arduino Nano implementation PRs to identify any uncovered acceptance gaps.\n2) Add focused regression tests for uncovered gap(s) rather than broad duplicate implementation.\n3) Submit minimal follow-up PR with `/claim #328` if gap exists.\n\nDecision gate: if maintainers confirm existing PRs already satisfy acceptance, I will pivot immediately to the next ROI-ranked target.\n","createdAt":"2026-03-16T17:26:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"SPAM","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4069350725","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF8878czEt","author":{"login":"mitchellecm7"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"\n/claim #328\n\nBuilt a full Arduino Nano in tscircuit including:\n- ATmega328P MCU (QFP32)\n- CH340G USB-to-serial converter\n- 16MHz + 12MHz crystals\n- Decoupling capacitors\n- Power, TX, RX LEDs with resistors\n- Mini-USB connector\n- Reset button with auto-reset capacitor\n- 3.3V voltage regulator\n- Digital (D0–D13) and Analog (A0–A5) header pins\n","createdAt":"2026-04-13T09:42:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4235407661","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABBh2Ygg","author":{"login":"chengyixu"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328 — Plan: Implement a complete Arduino Nano board definition using tscircuit, including all GPIO pins (D0-D13), analog pins (A0-A7), power pins (VIN, 5V, 3.3V, GND), USB/ICSP headers, ATmega328P footprint, and crystal oscillator. Will create the snippet on tscircuit.com and update the README with the link. Board will match the official Arduino Nano pinout specification.","createdAt":"2026-05-07T13:33:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4397570178","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABB-6JDg","author":{"login":"Bilal-Lodhi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #338\nI'm an AI-augmented developer. I've noted the requirements for the MCU, crystals, and capacitors. I'm starting a precision implementation of the Arduino Nano V3.0 now.","createdAt":"2026-05-12T06:53:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4428040462","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABB--73w","author":{"login":"dot-Justin"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nComplete Arduino Nano V3.0 implementation — ATmega328P-AU (TQFP-32) + CH340G + AMS1117-5.0/3.3 regulators + dual crystals (16 MHz/12 MHz) + DTR auto-reset + ICSP header + 4 status LEDs + full decoupling network. Board: 45 mm × 18 mm.\n\nPR: https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/3174","createdAt":"2026-05-12T07:04:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4428119007","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABB_nWpw","author":{"login":"Bilal-Lodhi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #328\n\nI have submitted a production-grade implementation in PR #3176.  \n\nThis version features:  \n- **44‑component BOM** – fully fabrication‑ready with precise MPNs  \n- **Dual‑regulator stage** – AMS1117‑5.0 + AMS1117‑3.3 with individual filtration  \n- **19 comprehensive tests** – validating every subsystem from AVCC filtration to DTR auto‑reset  \n\nCloses #328 ✅","createdAt":"2026-05-12T08:41:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4428781223","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABCURSlQ","author":{"login":"sayidilxs-web"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@iskhakov @algora-pbc\n\nHello Support Team,\n\nI hope you are doing well.\n\nI am writing regarding my rewarded bounty submissions, which are still pending even after 5 days.\n\nI carefully followed all contribution guidelines and completed the required work according to the platform rules. My submissions were reviewed, accepted, and successfully rewarded, and the related issues appear to be completed/closed.\n\nHere are my rewarded submissions:\n\nIssue / Bounty ID:  #3855\nReward Amount: $400\nSolution ID:  #4478\nSubmission Date: May 09, 2026\n\nIssue / Bounty ID: #3858\nReward Amount: $450\nSolution ID: #4476\nSubmission Date: May 09, 2026\n\nIssue / Bounty ID: #3218\nReward Amount: $150\nSolution ID: #4473\nSubmission Date: May 09, 2026\n\nTotal Reward Amount: $1000\n\nI have already completed all payout setup requirements, including connecting my Stripe account and adding my bank information correctly.\n\nThe bounty pages mention that payouts are generally processed within 2–5 days post-reward. Since 5 days have already passed, I kindly request you to review the payout status and release the pending payments.\n\nThank you very much for your time and support. I appreciate the opportunity to contribute to the project and I look forward to your response.\n\nBest regards,\nsayidilxs-web\n","createdAt":"2026-05-14T11:55:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4450439829","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABDfCjQA","author":{"login":"SimplyRayYZL"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nPlan: I’ll audit current main and the recent Arduino Nano bounty PRs before touching code, then only take a remaining acceptance gap. The likely review path is a small follow-up that improves correctness around pin aliases, power/reset/ICSP wiring, or fabrication metadata with focused tests and a tscircuit snippet/demo, instead of submitting another broad duplicate board implementation.","createdAt":"2026-05-24T13:23:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4528841536","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABDjyoJA","author":{"login":"kuaaq"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-05-25T11:17:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4533823524","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABDj8PLA","author":{"login":"kuaaq"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nComplete Arduino Nano V3.0 implementation:\n- ATmega328P-AU (TQFP-32) MCU\n- CH340G USB-serial bridge\n- AMS1117-5.0 / AMS1117-3.3 regulators\n- 16MHz crystal + 22pF caps\n- Auto-reset DTR circuit\n- ICSP header, LEDs, headers\n\nPR: https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/3263","createdAt":"2026-05-25T11:43:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4533980972","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABDk_RgQ","author":{"login":"justusaugust"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nI am taking a focused quality pass against current `main` and the latest open Arduino Nano PR. Plan:\n1. Build a complete Arduino Nano V3.0 snippet with explicit public header labels, ATmega328P + CH340G + regulators + reset/ICSP/USB/power/LED circuits, not just a decorative component list.\n2. Add tests that assert the board exposes the expected Nano pins and critical nets instead of relying only on a render.\n3. Update README with the snippet link/path.\n4. Include `/claim #328` in the PR body with local verification and a short proof/demo asset if the visual output is part of the review requirement.","createdAt":"2026-05-25T14:38:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4535079297","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABD9ZaMg","author":{"login":"gfgf-brain"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-05-28T03:45:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4560673330","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABD-ZHnA","author":{"login":"gfgf-brain"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-05-28T07:29:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4561717148","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABEW7D4Q","author":{"login":"khozakhulile27-netizen"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-05-31T17:06:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4587439073","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABEXFAzw","author":{"login":"chaudl113"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nComplete implementation with:\n- All components: ATmega328P, CH340G, dual AMS1117, dual crystals, USB Mini-B, LEDs, headers\n- 18 passing tests covering board, components, connectivity\n- PR: https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/3313","createdAt":"2026-05-31T18:08:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4587602127","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABEsS4EA","author":{"login":"gfgf-brain"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-06-03T06:56:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4609849360","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFaXaPw","author":{"login":"Aaloklovanshi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\nPlan: Design the Arduino Nano board using tscircuit (ATmega328P, CH340G, 16MHz crystal), publish it as a snippet, and update the README with the link.\nTools: Gemini CLI @AppData\\Local\\Packages\\MicrosoftWindows.Client.WebExperience_cw5n1h2txyewy\\LocalState\\EBWebView\\Default\\Network\\TransportSecurity + @cal.com\\agents\\rules\\quality-thorough-code-review.md\nAccount: Aaloklovanshi","createdAt":"2026-06-09T09:02:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4658158143","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFdu95g","author":{"login":"sourcesss"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nPlan: submit a focused README link to a public Arduino Nano V3.0 tscircuit project. The design models the ATmega328P-AU, CH340G USB-UART, Nano headers, ICSP, reset, crystals, power rails, and status LEDs, with a smoke test that renders circuit JSON via tscircuit. External project: https://github.com/sourcesss/arduino-nano-v3-tscircuit","createdAt":"2026-06-09T16:10:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4661689830","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFffOOA","author":{"login":"shauryam2807"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\nI have created a fully modular, manufacturing-ready 3-module design (ATmega328P + CH340G + Power/Headers) with all 83 traces correctly mapped. \n\nMy PR is ready here: #3417\n","createdAt":"2026-06-09T20:00:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4663529016","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFfyPdw","author":{"login":"nitin-rachabathuni"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Model Arduino Nano V3 (ATmega328P-AU + CH340G + Mini-USB) as modular tscircuit components under `examples/arduino-nano/`\n2. Wire all 30 header pins, ICSP, power rails, 16MHz + 12MHz crystals, auto-reset, and status LEDs with explicit traces\n3. Add smoke tests that render circuit JSON and validate board dimensions + component/trace count\n4. Link the example from README\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/pull/3418\n\nAll 3 tests pass locally (`bun test examples/arduino-nano/tests/arduino-nano.test.tsx`).","createdAt":"2026-06-09T20:43:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4663840631","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFf91ww","author":{"login":"nitin-rachabathuni"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"**Status update:** PR #3418 is green CI (test + smoke-init-test), mergeable, and includes 4 passing smoke tests.\n\n- Modular design: `ATmega328PCore`, `CH340GSerial`, `ArduinoNanoV3`\n- 31 components, 60+ traces, 18mm × 45mm board\n- README link + `examples/arduino-nano/README.md`\n\nReady for maintainer review when convenient.","createdAt":"2026-06-09T21:06:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tscircuit/tscircuit/issues/328#issuecomment-4664030659","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOLgfF888AAAABFhVWew","author":{"login":"Shaidyk"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #328","createdAt":"2026-06-10T00:53:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGrou